  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAPACITY IOM Somalia: Immigration and Borders (IB) 2024-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the auspices of the IOM-led Programme Pillar 1, IOM will implement activities to tackle the existing gaps in the civil registration of births and other life events to the benefits of migrants and the population at large. These interventions aim to inform various policies and strategies, providing the FGoS with essential data for effective governance and improved migration management. Technological advancements are another area that the project aims to support through the engagement of frontline officers in comprehensive user training sessions on data protection and border and migration management. Alongside, the provision of equipment aims to enhance their ability to provide effective and efficient services aligned with international standards.

By equipping institutions with the necessary tools and skills to support their policies, staff, administrative and operational capabilities, IOM remains committed to supporting regular migration pathways, reducing vulnerabilities and ensuring the protection of migrants&#x2019; rights. Overall, through a coordinated, multi-level approach, the proposed intervention in Somalia aims at tackling migration management challenges in a comprehensive and whole-of-government manner, in pursuit of the best development outcomes of Somalia, encompassing economic, social and political aspects.</narrative>
  </description>
